From 04e1770dce68e3f3021d45c6105938fb35d509e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 21:23:38 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Tell mpv the packing of a 3D video that does not declare
 it

A stream that carries the frame packing SEI or Matroska's StereoMode is
unpacked by mpv itself. Videos from Invidious and Piped often carry
neither, and YouTube's 3D uploads were marked with keywords instead:
yt3d:enable=LR, RL, LonR and RonL, yt3d:swap=true, and in the first
form yt3d:left and yt3d:right. Read these from the video's keywords
and, when the stream says nothing about 3D, give mpv the packing as the
stereo-in parameter of a format filter.

A video that carries neither a declaration nor such keywords is taken
for side by side when the frame is at least 2.5 times as wide as high,
as mpv decides it: no single picture is that wide. Top and bottom is
not guessed.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet via Claude Code
